# P49 — IMMERSIVE VR DESIGN REVIEW
## End-to-End Implementation Specification — Plotify Account B

**Roadmap ID:** P49  
**Feature:** Immersive VR Design Review  
**Product:** Plotify — Architecture Intelligence Platform  
**Implementation mode:** Inspect → Plan → Implement → Verify → Report  
**Primary objective:** Enable users to inspect existing Plotify architectural models in an immersive virtual-reality environment, explore spatial relationships at meaningful scales, identify and annotate design issues, and preserve review state safely.

---

# 1. MISSION AND EXPECTED USER OUTCOME

Implement P49 as a complete, coherent VR design-review workspace integrated into the existing Plotify application.

The goal is to help users understand a design in three dimensions in ways that may be difficult through a flat screen: room proportions, circulation, spatial relationships, building form, terrain context, and the location of potential design concerns.

P49 must deliver more than a VR launch button. It should provide a usable workflow from project selection to immersive inspection, navigation, issue marking, saved review notes, exit, and follow-up inspection.

The user should be able to:

1. Select a valid Plotify project and reviewable design.
2. inspect the available 3D model and understand its geometry, units, limitations, and source information.
3. Enter an immersive VR session when the device, browser, security context, and runtime support it.
4. Explore a building at a clearly labelled full-scale or model-scale setting where supported by model data.
5. Navigate with VR controllers or another genuinely supported interaction method.
6. Switch between useful architectural review layers without losing context.
7. Mark a design location, create a review note, and inspect the note later.
8. Identify stale or unavailable analysis data.
9. Exit VR safely and return to a usable standard 3D review.
10. Preserve saved review information across appropriate project reloads.

The feature must distinguish an immersive visual review from a certified survey, a construction set-out tool, a code-compliance engine, or a validated structural, environmental, or building-performance simulation.

## Success principle

Make the model easier to understand, the review easier to perform, and the limitations easier to see. Do not fabricate measurements, model detail, physical-world alignment, or engineering certainty to make the VR experience look more impressive.

